  "reasoning": "The defendants set traps, illegally captured four golden snub‑nosed monkeys (a protected endangered species) and sold them. This constitutes illegal hunting of precious, endangered wildlife, which under Chinese criminal law is the crime of illegal hunting/capturing of protected wildlife. The prosecution explicitly states the charge as ‘非法猎捕珍贵、濒危野生动物罪’. No other distinct offenses (e.g., theft) are present, so the appropriate charge is this single crime.",
